      "writtenOn": "2025-06-03T12:48:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should move away from a full URL for the changelog for the same reasons as we did for the zips, at least for now.\n\nBut this reminds me: if we ever change something like this, how do we maintain compatibility for older updaters? Is that where adding /v2/ or something to the URL for the new updaters comes into play?",
      "parentUuid": "21ad2b96_a5c25e7c",
      "revId": "b71d4c1f7228b197102ed059a0bdb95ae7b30328",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09cfddff_b8e15bbb",
        "filename": "sample-metadata.json",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-03T15:56:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need a /v2/ for most things.\n\nUnless we change what the same variable means, we can easily maintain backwards compatibility by using new variables.\n\nToday: changelog_url\nTomorrow: changelog_filepath\nLater: changelog_contents\n\netc.\n\nAnd in the Updater we\u0027d have to retain support for the above, and gradually remove it. Some work there, but less work than having to deal with a new URL or version, as that then indirectly forces an update path when not needed.",
      "parentUuid": "191e916f_c18b890a",
      "revId": "b71d4c1f7228b197102ed059a0bdb95ae7b30328",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    }
